  "preamble": "Spontaneous diphthongization of stressed open [ɔ] (from Latin short ŏ) to a rising diphthong [we] is a hallmark of Spanish and neighbouring Ibero-Romance varieties, and Old French shows a parallel ue diphthong. Italian took the same path only as far as [wɔ] (see o→uo).",
